d (deities), and Nāgas, and Yaksas, and Gandharvas, and Asuras, and Maharsis. And, for certain, they have herein tried to do us some wrong. Therefore there is no doubt about this, do you by main force take him. And, you generals, go you taking a mighty force with steeds, elephants and cars. Do you chastise this monkey.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.443,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-46-6","DUTT-5-46-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5044008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4e220026461af24b002877126b98f358abc41ff46da879077745816a73730f40","compact":"fb0777d74c977813c10e53495dd079ed4b74fbfc3f36c4f6c023bc5f9a753472","nasal":"fb0777d74c977813c10e53495dd079ed4b74fbfc3f36c4f6c023bc5f9a753472"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-44-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":44,"verse":9,"english":"This monkey of deliberate prowess should not be disregarded by you. I have seen (There is a word sighra, soon-in this Śloka, of which I fail to perceive the relation) monkeys of immense prowess, Vāli with Sugrīva and the exceedingly powerful Jāmbavāna, and Nīla the general, and others with Dwivida at their head.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.623,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-46-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5044009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d4a5b22a629a8090ef4e20602a51094c97945fc739cb56a9b9b91a4c80cd6536","compact":"275176b82d2a8bd85a44786ca907aafcc6ef3f4cd9ba698768bb1dde83765df2","nasal":"275176b82d2a8bd85a44786ca907aafcc6ef3f4cd9ba698768bb1dde83765df2"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-44-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":44,"verse":10,"english":"This monkey of deliberate prowess should not be disregarded by you. I have seen (There is a word sighra, soon-in this Śloka, of which I fail to perceive the relation) monkeys of immense prowess, Vāli with 