e earth with the violence of the Fair-feathered (bird).* (Suparna-a name of Garuda.)","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.556,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-46-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5044029","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"47a8cf44b459dc4d9660d25fbf4d894ac3db3e582e366b866c404e77c5b58529","compact":"1772cfc1acdd6dbac8ba6d3597e62dcec9f1b916b535a973b93c06ae2f9a8735","nasal":"1772cfc1acdd6dbac8ba6d3597e62dcec9f1b916b535a973b93c06ae2f9a8735"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-44-30","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":44,"verse":30,"english":"Then getting at and uprooting a sāla tree, that monkey, the Wind-god's offspring, slew both of those heroic Rākşasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-46-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5044030","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"38a184fbd2f8a9957946eada53da6482f1ed30031a5d17385948bf93661128d9","compact":"20991961200aab402bf5b8ce52c5a907b7bc06b1f629232f30438c6edde951b1","nasal":"20991961200aab402bf5b8ce52c5a907b7bc06b1f629232f30438c6edde951b1"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-44-31","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":44,"verse":31,"english":"Learning that those three had been slain by the monkey gifted with speed, the mighty and onrushing Praghasa laughing in scorn advanced (in the encounter). And the energetic Bhāsakarņa also came forward in rage, taking a dart. And (they) meeting together, Praghasa assailed the famous, tiger-like monkey with a sharp-edged axe, and Bhāsakarņa (attacked) the elephantine monkey with a javelin.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.507,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-46-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5044031","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{